      "module": "_comment_anthropic_sdk_closure",
      "version": "spec-1.20: github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-go@v1.45.0 (direct, allow-listed above) is a SINGLE module bundling Anthropic + AWS Bedrock + GCP Vertex + MCP backends. MVS pulls its full require closure into `go list -m all`, but `go mod why` confirms NONE of the AWS/GCP/MCP/otel modules below are compiled into the opendbx binary — only the Claude Messages API path is imported. These are module-graph / go.sum supply-chain surface only (not runtime deps). Investigated (spec-1.20 R-fix B): no SDK version since v1.25.0 drops AWS/GCP; bedrock/vertex are same-module subpackages so build-tag/replace cannot prune them; the closure is inherent to the SDK's single-module multi-backend design. Accepted per user path-3/3 (option A); narrowing to a hand-rolled minimal client deferred to spec-1.20.1 / 3.x if dep policy tightens."
    },
